\section*{Question 1}
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Volume } & =\int_{0}^{10} A(h) d h \\
& \approx(2-0) \cdot A(0)+(5-2) \cdot A(2)+(10-5) \cdot A(5) \\
& =2 \cdot 50.3+3 \cdot 14.4+5 \cdot 6.5 \\
& =176.3 \text { cubic feet }
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)] The approximation in part (a) is an overestimate because a left Riemann sum is used and \(A\) is decreasing.
\item[(c)] \(\int_{0}^{10} f(h) d h=101.325338\)
The volume is 101.325 cubic feet.
\item[1] : units in parts (a), (c), and (d)
